---
import { url } from '../lib/base';
const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/openshield-org/openshield';
---

<section class="sec-rule" id="start">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>New here? Run it in this order.</h2>
      <a class="sec-link" href="https://openshieldlearn.netlify.app/learn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn portal &#8594;</a>
    </div>
    <div class="journey">
      <a class="jcard" href={url('/docs/')}><span class="jno">01</span><h3>Set up read-only access</h3><p>Authenticate, choose the subscription scope and understand where findings will be stored.</p><span class="jlink">On-site quickstart <span class="ar">&#8594;</span></span></a>
      <a class="jcard" href={url('/docs/')}><span class="jno">02</span><h3>Run your first scan</h3><p>Load the repository-derived rule set and produce a posture report you can trace.</p><span class="jlink">Run the commands <span class="ar">&#8594;</span></span></a>
      <a class="jcard" href={url('/rules/')}><span class="jno">03</span><h3>Read your findings</h3><p>Every finding names the control it violates and carries the exact CLI command that fixes it.</p><span class="jlink">Rules reference <span class="ar">&#8594;</span></span></a>
      <a class="jcard" href="https://openshield-gules.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="jno">04</span><h3>Explore the dashboard</h3><p>Review findings, drift and compliance when the hosted API is available, or connect your own deployment.</p><span class="jlink">Hosted dashboard <span class="ar">&#8594;</span></span></a>
      <a class="jcard" href={`${GITHUB}/blob/dev/docs/adding-a-rule.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="jno">05</span><h3>Ship your own rule</h3><p>Add a misconfiguration check in under 30 minutes. Students and first-timers welcome.</p><span class="jlink">adding-a-rule.md <span class="ar">&#8594;</span></span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
